ccpthread.lib/--background--                      ccpthread.lib/--background--

    ccpthread.lib is a static companion to cclib.library: POSIX threads,
    mutexes, condition variables, rwlocks, TLS keys, cooperative cancel,
    pthread_once, and unnamed POSIX semaphores.  Port of unix.lib2
    pthread.lib with CClib session deltas only.

    Process model
	Each pthread is an Amiga Process (CreateNewProc).  Parent and child
	handshake through the child's MsgPort Signal bit.
	Asm entry _cc_pthread_startup reloads A4 from _LinkerDB, then calls
	_cc_thread_entry; workers return via rts (no dos Exit — no CLI).

    CClib session
	Workers call SetupSTDIO with FILE* slots on the ThreadPair so CRT
	globals stdin/stdout/stderr (parent) are not overwritten.  Session
	thr_ctx / thr_teardown run from ClearSTDIO (TLS destructors need
	app A4 — run via __saveds / cc_geta4).  ClearSTDIO re-entry latch
	is per-session, not library-global.  Blocking waits (join / cond /
	sem / timed) and mutex_lock poll Ctrl-C so abort_func can force
	a panic.  Never leave a ThreadPair in tc_UserData across CClib LVOs.

    Stdio
	Workers inherit the parent's Input/Output (NP_Close* FALSE) so
	printf goes to the same console.  Use printf / puts (session
	stdout_p).  Do not pass CRT globals stdin/stdout/stderr into
	fflush / fclose / etc. on a worker — those FILE* belong to the
	parent session and will panic (code 20).  Avoid concurrent
	printf/fflush from multiple threads on the shared console;
	dos.library Write is not safely reentrant on one CON:.

    Sync waits
	Condition and semaphore waits use AllocSignal, not pr_MsgPort
	(shared with DOS / create handshake).

    Limits / not implemented
	PTHREAD_THREADS_MAX 64, PTHREAD_KEYS_MAX 32, PTHREAD_STACK_MIN 8192.
	Cooperative cancel only (ASYNCHRONOUS stored, not honoured).  No
	cleanup_push/pop, named sem_open, or SysV semget (those are outside
	unix.lib2 pthread.lib).  Mutex kind NORMAL rejects same-task relock.

    SEE ALSO
	pthread.h, semaphore.h, cclib.library/--background--

ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_init                ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_init
   NAME
	pthread_attr_init -- initialize thread attributes

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_attr_init(pthread_attr_t *attr);

   FUNCTION
	Fills attr with defaults: joinable, stack size PTHREAD_STACK_MIN.

   INPUTS
	attr - attribute object to initialize

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if attr is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_attr_destroy, pthread_create

ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_destroy          ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_destroy
   NAME
	pthread_attr_destroy -- destroy thread attributes

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_attr_destroy(pthread_attr_t *attr);

   FUNCTION
	Marks the attribute object unused.  Safe to call after create.

   INPUTS
	attr - attribute object

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if attr is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_attr_init

ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_setdetachstate
				  ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_setdetachstate
   NAME
	pthread_attr_setdetachstate -- joinable or detached create

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_attr_setdetachstate(pthread_attr_t *attr, int state);

   FUNCTION
	Sets PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE (0) or PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED (1).
	Detached threads free their ThreadPair when finished; joinable
	threads require pthread_join (or detach later).

   INPUTS
	attr  - attribute object
	state - PTHREAD_CREATE_JOINABLE or PTHREAD_CREATE_DETACHED

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL on bad attr or state.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_attr_getdetachstate, pthread_detach, pthread_join

ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_getdetachstate
				  ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_getdetachstate
   NAME
	pthread_attr_getdetachstate -- read detach state

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_attr_getdetachstate(const pthread_attr_t *attr,
	    int *state);

   FUNCTION
	Stores the current detach state in *state.

   INPUTS
	attr  - attribute object
	state - out: detach state

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if attr or state is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_attr_setdetachstate

ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_setstacksize    ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_setstacksize
   NAME
	pthread_attr_setstacksize -- set CreateNewProc stack size

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_attr_setstacksize(pthread_attr_t *attr, size_t stacksize);

   FUNCTION
	Sets NP_StackSize for the worker Process.  Values below
	PTHREAD_STACK_MIN are raised to the minimum at create time.

   INPUTS
	attr      - attribute object
	stacksize - bytes of stack

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if attr is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_attr_getstacksize, pthread_create

ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_getstacksize    ccpthread.lib/pthread_attr_getstacksize
   NAME
	pthread_attr_getstacksize -- read stack size attribute

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_attr_getstacksize(const pthread_attr_t *attr,
	    size_t *stacksize);

   FUNCTION
	Stores the configured stack size in *stacksize.

   INPUTS
	attr      - attribute object
	stacksize - out: stack size

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if attr or stacksize is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_attr_setstacksize

ccpthread.lib/pthread_create                      ccpthread.lib/pthread_create
   NAME
	pthread_create -- start a worker Process as a pthread

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_create(pthread_t *thread, const pthread_attr_t *attr,
	    void *(*start_routine)(void *), void *arg);

   FUNCTION
	Allocates a ThreadPair, CreateNewProc with entry
	_cc_pthread_startup, inherits parent Input/Output, Signals the
	child to run.  The worker clears the pair from tc_UserData,
	SetupSTDIO, installs thr_ctx / abort, then calls start_routine.
	On normal return or pthread_exit, ClearSTDIO runs and joiners
	are Signal'd.  Abort / panic / Ctrl-C on the worker RemTask after
	waking joiners (result PTHREAD_CANCELED).

   INPUTS
	thread        - out: new pthread_t id
	attr          - optional attributes (NULL = joinable, min stack)
	start_routine - thread entry
	arg           - argument to start_routine

   RESULT
	0 on success.  EAGAIN if AllocMem / AllocSignal / CreateNewProc
	fails.  EINVAL if thread or start_routine is NULL.

   NOTES
	Caller must already have an active CClib session (CRT SetupSTDIO).
	start_routine near-BSS needs A4; the lib invokes via a __saveds
	trampoline after SetupSTDIO (which leaves A4 trashed).

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_join, pthread_detach, pthread_exit, SetupSTDIO

ccpthread.lib/pthread_join                          ccpthread.lib/pthread_join
   NAME
	pthread_join -- wait for a joinable thread to finish

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_join(pthread_t thread, void **retval);

   FUNCTION
	Blocks until the target ThreadPair sets finished, then optionally
	stores the exit value in *retval and frees the pair.  Uses the
	parent_sig allocated at create.

   INPUTS
	thread - id from pthread_create
	retval - optional out: start_routine / pthread_exit value

   RESULT
	0 on success.  ESRCH if unknown id.  EINVAL if detached or
	self-join.  EDEADLK if joining self.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_create, pthread_detach, pthread_exit

ccpthread.lib/pthread_detach                      ccpthread.lib/pthread_detach
   NAME
	pthread_detach -- mark a thread for automatic cleanup

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_detach(pthread_t thread);

   FUNCTION
	Marks the ThreadPair detached.  If already finished, frees it
	immediately; otherwise the worker frees itself on exit.

   INPUTS
	thread - id from pthread_create

   RESULT
	0 on success.  ESRCH / EINVAL on bad or already-detached id.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_join, pthread_attr_setdetachstate

ccpthread.lib/pthread_exit                          ccpthread.lib/pthread_exit
   NAME
	pthread_exit -- terminate the calling thread

   SYNOPSIS
	void pthread_exit(void *retval);

   FUNCTION
	On a worker: stores retval, ClearSTDIO, Signals the joiner,
	frees if detached, then returns to asm (RemTask via process
	exit).  On the main thread: sets result and returns (does not
	exit the process).

   INPUTS
	retval - value visible to pthread_join

   RESULT
	Does not return on a worker Process.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_join, ClearSTDIO

ccpthread.lib/pthread_self                          ccpthread.lib/pthread_self
   NAME
	pthread_self -- id of the calling thread

   SYNOPSIS
	pthread_t pthread_self(void);

   FUNCTION
	Returns the ThreadPair id for the current session (thr_ctx),
	creating a main-thread pair if needed.

   INPUTS
	None.

   RESULT
	pthread_t id (never zero for a live pair in this implementation).

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_equal, pthread_create

ccpthread.lib/pthread_equal                        ccpthread.lib/pthread_equal
   NAME
	pthread_equal -- compare thread ids

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_equal(pthread_t t1, pthread_t t2);

   FUNCTION
	Returns non-zero if t1 and t2 are the same id.

   INPUTS
	t1, t2 - thread ids

   RESULT
	Non-zero if equal, zero otherwise.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_self

ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_init              ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_init
   NAME
	pthread_mutex_init -- initialize a mutex

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_mutex_init(pthread_mutex_t *mutex,
	    const pthread_mutexattr_t *attr);

   FUNCTION
	InitSemaphore on the embedded SignalSemaphore.  attr may be NULL;
	kind defaults to PTHREAD_MUTEX_NORMAL (RECURSIVE reserved).

   INPUTS
	mutex - mutex object
	attr  - optional attributes (kind)

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if mutex is NULL.

   NOTES
	PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER is also supported for static init.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_mutex_destroy, pthread_mutex_lock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_destroy        ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_destroy
   NAME
	pthread_mutex_destroy -- destroy a mutex

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_mutex_destroy(pthread_mutex_t *mutex);

   FUNCTION
	Fails with EBUSY if waiters are present.  Otherwise leaves the
	object inert.

   INPUTS
	mutex - mutex object

   RESULT
	0, EINVAL, or EBUSY.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_mutex_init

ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_lock              ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_lock
   NAME
	pthread_mutex_lock -- lock a mutex

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_mutex_lock(pthread_mutex_t *mutex);

   FUNCTION
	ObtainSemaphore on the embedded SignalSemaphore.

   INPUTS
	mutex - mutex object

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if mutex is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_mutex_trylock, pthread_mutex_unlock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_trylock        ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_trylock
   NAME
	pthread_mutex_trylock -- non-blocking lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_mutex_trylock(pthread_mutex_t *mutex);

   FUNCTION
	AttemptSemaphore; returns EBUSY if the mutex is held.

   INPUTS
	mutex - mutex object

   RESULT
	0, EBUSY, or EINVAL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_mutex_lock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_timedlock    ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_timedlock
   NAME
	pthread_mutex_timedlock -- lock with absolute timeout

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_mutex_timedlock(pthread_mutex_t *mutex,
	    const struct timespec *abstime);

   FUNCTION
	Polls AttemptSemaphore until success or abstime (CLOCK wall via
	time()).  Returns ETIMEDOUT on expiry.

   INPUTS
	mutex   - mutex object
	abstime - absolute timeout

   RESULT
	0, ETIMEDOUT, EINVAL, or EAGAIN.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_mutex_lock, pthread_cond_timedwait

ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_unlock          ccpthread.lib/pthread_mutex_unlock
   NAME
	pthread_mutex_unlock -- unlock a mutex

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_mutex_unlock(pthread_mutex_t *mutex);

   FUNCTION
	ReleaseSemaphore on the embedded SignalSemaphore.

   INPUTS
	mutex - mutex object

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if mutex is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_mutex_lock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_init                ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_init
   NAME
	pthread_cond_init -- initialize a condition variable

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_cond_init(pthread_cond_t *cond,
	    const pthread_condattr_t *attr);

   FUNCTION
	InitSemaphore and empty waiter list.  attr is ignored (reserved).

   INPUTS
	cond - condition object
	attr - optional (may be NULL)

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if cond is NULL.

   NOTES
	PTHREAD_COND_INITIALIZER is supported for static init.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cond_wait, pthread_cond_signal

ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_destroy          ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_destroy
   NAME
	pthread_cond_destroy -- destroy a condition variable

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_cond_destroy(pthread_cond_t *cond);

   FUNCTION
	Fails with EBUSY if waiters remain.

   INPUTS
	cond - condition object

   RESULT
	0, EINVAL, or EBUSY.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cond_init

ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_wait                ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_wait
   NAME
	pthread_cond_wait -- wait on a condition variable

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_cond_wait(pthread_cond_t *cond, pthread_mutex_t *mutex);

   FUNCTION
	Atomically releases mutex and waits on an AllocSignal bit until
	signal/broadcast.  Re-acquires mutex before return.  Spurious
	wakeups are possible; callers must re-check the predicate.

   INPUTS
	cond  - condition object
	mutex - mutex held by the caller

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL on bad args, EAGAIN if AllocSignal fails.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cond_timedwait, pthread_cond_signal, pthread_cond_broadcast

ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_timedwait      ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_timedwait
   NAME
	pthread_cond_timedwait -- timed condition wait

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_cond_timedwait(pthread_cond_t *cond,
	    pthread_mutex_t *mutex, const struct timespec *abstime);

   FUNCTION
	Like pthread_cond_wait with absolute timeout via timer.device
	UNIT_VBLANK.  Mutex is held again on return (including timeout).

   INPUTS
	cond    - condition object
	mutex   - mutex held by the caller
	abstime - absolute timeout

   RESULT
	0, ETIMEDOUT, EINVAL, or EAGAIN.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cond_wait

ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_signal            ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_signal
   NAME
	pthread_cond_signal -- wake one waiter

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_cond_signal(pthread_cond_t *cond);

   FUNCTION
	Signals one waiter on the condition list, if any.

   INPUTS
	cond - condition object

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if cond is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cond_broadcast, pthread_cond_wait

ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_broadcast      ccpthread.lib/pthread_cond_broadcast
   NAME
	pthread_cond_broadcast -- wake all waiters

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_cond_broadcast(pthread_cond_t *cond);

   FUNCTION
	Signals every waiter currently on the condition list.

   INPUTS
	cond - condition object

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if cond is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cond_signal

ccpthread.lib/pthread_once                          ccpthread.lib/pthread_once
   NAME
	pthread_once -- one-time initialization

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_once(pthread_once_t *once_control,
	    void (*init_routine)(void));

   FUNCTION
	Calls init_routine exactly once across all threads for a given
	once_control (PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT).  Concurrent callers serialize
	on an internal SignalSemaphore.

   INPUTS
	once_control - once object
	init_routine - function to run once

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if once_control or init_routine is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_create

ccpthread.lib/sem_init                                  ccpthread.lib/sem_init
   NAME
	sem_init -- initialize an unnamed semaphore

   SYNOPSIS
	int sem_init(sem_t *sem, int pshared, unsigned int value);

   FUNCTION
	Creates an unnamed counting semaphore (SignalSemaphore + waiter
	list).  pshared must be 0 (process-shared not supported).  value
	must be <= SEM_VALUE_MAX.

   INPUTS
	sem     - semaphore object
	pshared - must be 0
	value   - initial count

   RESULT
	0 on success.  On failure returns -1 and sets errno (EINVAL,
	ENOSYS for pshared != 0).

   SEE ALSO
	sem_destroy, sem_wait, sem_post

ccpthread.lib/sem_destroy                            ccpthread.lib/sem_destroy
   NAME
	sem_destroy -- destroy an unnamed semaphore

   SYNOPSIS
	int sem_destroy(sem_t *sem);

   FUNCTION
	Fails if waiters are present (EBUSY).

   INPUTS
	sem - semaphore object

   RESULT
	0 on success, -1 with errno on failure.

   SEE ALSO
	sem_init

ccpthread.lib/sem_wait                                  ccpthread.lib/sem_wait
   NAME
	sem_wait -- decrement semaphore (block)

   SYNOPSIS
	int sem_wait(sem_t *sem);

   FUNCTION
	If value > 0, decrements and returns.  Otherwise waits on an
	AllocSignal bit until sem_post.

   INPUTS
	sem - semaphore object

   RESULT
	0 on success, -1 with errno on failure.

   SEE ALSO
	sem_trywait, sem_timedwait, sem_post

ccpthread.lib/sem_trywait                            ccpthread.lib/sem_trywait
   NAME
	sem_trywait -- non-blocking decrement

   SYNOPSIS
	int sem_trywait(sem_t *sem);

   FUNCTION
	Decrements if value > 0; otherwise fails with EAGAIN.

   INPUTS
	sem - semaphore object

   RESULT
	0 on success, -1 with errno (EAGAIN / EINVAL).

   SEE ALSO
	sem_wait

ccpthread.lib/sem_timedwait                        ccpthread.lib/sem_timedwait
   NAME
	sem_timedwait -- decrement with absolute timeout

   SYNOPSIS
	int sem_timedwait(sem_t *sem, const struct timespec *abstime);

   FUNCTION
	Like sem_wait with absolute timeout (timer.device).

   INPUTS
	sem     - semaphore object
	abstime - absolute timeout

   RESULT
	0 on success, -1 with errno (ETIMEDOUT / EINVAL / EAGAIN).

   SEE ALSO
	sem_wait

ccpthread.lib/sem_post                                  ccpthread.lib/sem_post
   NAME
	sem_post -- increment semaphore / wake one waiter

   SYNOPSIS
	int sem_post(sem_t *sem);

   FUNCTION
	Increments value or wakes one waiter.  Fails with EOVERFLOW if
	value would exceed SEM_VALUE_MAX.

   INPUTS
	sem - semaphore object

   RESULT
	0 on success, -1 with errno on failure.

   SEE ALSO
	sem_wait

ccpthread.lib/sem_getvalue                          ccpthread.lib/sem_getvalue
   NAME
	sem_getvalue -- read current count

   SYNOPSIS
	int sem_getvalue(sem_t *sem, int *sval);

   FUNCTION
	Stores the current value in *sval (non-negative; waiters do not
	make the count negative in this implementation).

   INPUTS
	sem  - semaphore object
	sval - out: current value

   RESULT
	0 on success, -1 with errno on failure.

   SEE ALSO
	sem_init, sem_post

ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_init                ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_init
   NAME
	pthread_rwlock_init -- initialize a read-write lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_rwlock_init(pthread_rwlock_t *rwlock,
	    const pthread_rwlockattr_t *attr);

   FUNCTION
	Port of unix.lib2: mutex + reader/writer condition variables.

   RESULT
	0 on success, EINVAL if rwlock is NULL.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_rwlock_rdlock, pthread_rwlock_wrlock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_destroy          ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_destroy
   NAME
	pthread_rwlock_destroy -- destroy a read-write lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_rwlock_destroy(pthread_rwlock_t *rwlock);

   RESULT
	0, EINVAL, or EBUSY if holders remain.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_rwlock_init

ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_rdlock            ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_rdlock
   NAME
	pthread_rwlock_rdlock -- shared read lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_rwlock_rdlock(pthread_rwlock_t *rwlock);

   FUNCTION
	Waits while writers are active or waiting.  Cancel point.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_rwlock_tryrdlock, pthread_rwlock_unlock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_tryrdlock      ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_tryrdlock
   NAME
	pthread_rwlock_tryrdlock -- non-blocking read lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_rwlock_tryrdlock(pthread_rwlock_t *rwlock);

   RESULT
	0 or EBUSY.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_rwlock_rdlock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_wrlock            ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_wrlock
   NAME
	pthread_rwlock_wrlock -- exclusive write lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_rwlock_wrlock(pthread_rwlock_t *rwlock);

   FUNCTION
	Waits for all readers and writers.  Cancel point.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_rwlock_trywrlock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_trywrlock      ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_trywrlock
   NAME
	pthread_rwlock_trywrlock -- non-blocking write lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_rwlock_trywrlock(pthread_rwlock_t *rwlock);

   RESULT
	0 or EBUSY.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_rwlock_wrlock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_unlock            ccpthread.lib/pthread_rwlock_unlock
   NAME
	pthread_rwlock_unlock -- unlock a read-write lock

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_rwlock_unlock(pthread_rwlock_t *rwlock);

   FUNCTION
	Releases a held read or write lock; prefers waiting writers.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_rwlock_rdlock, pthread_rwlock_wrlock

ccpthread.lib/pthread_key_create              ccpthread.lib/pthread_key_create
   NAME
	pthread_key_create -- allocate a TLS key

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_key_create(pthread_key_t *key, void (*destructor)(void *));

   FUNCTION
	Allocates a key slot (PTHREAD_KEYS_MAX).  destructor may be NULL.
	Destructors run from ClearSTDIO thr_teardown (one pass).

   RESULT
	0, EINVAL, or EAGAIN if the key table is full.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_setspecific, pthread_key_delete

ccpthread.lib/pthread_key_delete              ccpthread.lib/pthread_key_delete
   NAME
	pthread_key_delete -- free a TLS key

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_key_delete(pthread_key_t key);

   FUNCTION
	Marks the key unused.  Does not run destructors for existing values.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_key_create

ccpthread.lib/pthread_setspecific            ccpthread.lib/pthread_setspecific
   NAME
	pthread_setspecific -- store a TLS value for this thread

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_setspecific(pthread_key_t key, const void *value);

   FUNCTION
	Stores value on the current ThreadPair (via thr_ctx).

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_getspecific

ccpthread.lib/pthread_getspecific            ccpthread.lib/pthread_getspecific
   NAME
	pthread_getspecific -- fetch this thread's TLS value

   SYNOPSIS
	void *pthread_getspecific(pthread_key_t key);

   RESULT
	Stored pointer, or NULL if unset / bad key / no ThreadPair.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_setspecific

ccpthread.lib/pthread_cancel                      ccpthread.lib/pthread_cancel
   NAME
	pthread_cancel -- request cooperative cancellation

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_cancel(pthread_t thread);

   FUNCTION
	Marks CANCEL_REQUESTED.  Target exits at the next cancel point
	(pthread_testcancel, mutex_lock, cond_wait, …) via
	pthread_exit(PTHREAD_CANCELED).

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_testcancel, pthread_setcancelstate

ccpthread.lib/pthread_testcancel              ccpthread.lib/pthread_testcancel
   NAME
	pthread_testcancel -- cancel point

   SYNOPSIS
	void pthread_testcancel(void);

   FUNCTION
	If cancel enabled and requested, pthread_exit(PTHREAD_CANCELED).

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cancel

ccpthread.lib/pthread_setcancelstate      ccpthread.lib/pthread_setcancelstate
   NAME
	pthread_setcancelstate -- enable or disable cancellation

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_setcancelstate(int state, int *oldstate);

   FUNCTION
	PTHREAD_CANCEL_ENABLE or PTHREAD_CANCEL_DISABLE.

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_cancel, pthread_setcanceltype

ccpthread.lib/pthread_setcanceltype        ccpthread.lib/pthread_setcanceltype
   NAME
	pthread_setcanceltype -- deferred vs asynchronous

   SYNOPSIS
	int pthread_setcanceltype(int type, int *oldtype);

   FUNCTION
	Stores the type.  Only cooperative deferred cancel is honoured
	(ASYNCHRONOUS is accepted but not implemented).

   SEE ALSO
	pthread_setcancelstate

